{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.JonesMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.JonesMarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3AlgebraLaws"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.jonesMarkov_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.jonesMarkov_H3","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L246-L264","doc":"**Jones–Markov trace on `H₃(q)`** (repaired form, sorry-free):\nnormalisation, cyclicity, the Markov property on `H₂`, and the negative\nstabilisation with `z₋ = z − h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.mulσ₁_mulσ₁Inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.mulσ₁_mulσ₁Inv","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L241-L244","doc":"`σ₁⁻¹ = σ₁ − h` is a right inverse of `σ₁`: `(x σ₁⁻¹) σ₁ = x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.mulσ₁Inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.mulσ₁Inv","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L238-L239","doc":"`x · σ₁⁻¹` on the NF module, using `σ₁⁻¹ = σ₁ − h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.not_forall_jonesMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.not_forall_jonesMarkovTrace","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L199-L216","doc":"**No Jones–Markov trace exists on unconstrained `HeckeAlgebraData`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.q_param_ne_q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.q_param_ne_q_inv_param","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L192-L197","doc":"`q ≠ q⁻¹` in `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.markov_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.markov_neg","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L168-L168","doc":"**Negative stabilisation (Markov II input)**:\ntr(x · T_{n-1}⁻¹) = z₋ · tr(x) with z₋ = z − (q − q⁻¹).\nCombined with tr_comm (Markov I), markov_pos, and the\nwrithe-normalisation prefactor of Jones 1987 §5, this ensures\nthe normalised invariant depends only on the isotopy class of\nthe braid closure, yielding the Jones polynomial J_L(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.z_neg_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.z_neg_spec","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L159-L159","doc":"`z_neg` is pinned to its Hecke-forced value z − (q − q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.z_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.z_neg","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L156-L156","doc":"Negative-crossing loop value `z₋ = z − (q − q⁻¹)`.\n\nForced by linearity and the Hecke quadratic relation\nσ⁻¹ = σ − (q − q⁻¹): substituting into `markov_pos` gives\ntr(x·T⁻¹) = (z − (q − q⁻¹))·tr(x). Note z₋ ≠ z for q ≠ ±1,\nand z₋ is NOT z⁻¹ — the two stabilisations do not scale by\nmutually inverse factors for any non-degenerate trace\nparameter (z·z₋ = 1 forces z ∈ {q, −q⁻¹}, the two\none-dimensional characters). Link invariance is restored by\nthe writhe prefactor outside the trace (Jones 1987 §5), not\nby ±-symmetry of the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.nondeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.nondeg","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L141-L141","doc":"**Non-degeneracy (weak form)**: the trace is not identically zero.\nThe index `i` does not enter the body, so this field says only that\nsome element has nonzero trace; it does **not** encode \"nonzero on\nevery irreducible `S_λ`\". That stronger reading would also be false\nunder convention D, where the Ocneanu weight of every shape with a\nthird row vanishes. A per-`S_λ` statement needs the Wedderburn\ndecomposition, which this structure does not carry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.numIrreps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.numIrreps","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L131-L131","doc":"Number of irreducible summands at level n (= ⌊n/2⌋ + 1 for SU_q(2)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.markov_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.markov_pos","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L124-L124","doc":"**Markov property** (positive stabilisation):\ntr(x · T_{n-1}) = z · tr(x) for x ∈ H_n(q).\nThis encodes vertical stabilisation in the Hecke tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.z_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.z_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L119-L119","doc":"The Markov parameter is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.z","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L116-L116","doc":"Markov-trace loop value `z = tr_M(σ_i)`. The canonical value is\nconvention D, `z = q³/(q² + 1)` (owner ruling 2026-08-15), which\nis what the `.md` statement fixes. This structure leaves `z` free:\nthe pin is **not** encoded here, so nothing proved from this\nstructure depends on convention D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.tr_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.tr_comm","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L109-L109","doc":"Trace property (cyclicity): tr(ab) = tr(ba). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.tr_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.tr_one","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L106-L106","doc":"Normalisation: tr(1) = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.tr","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The trace functional tr_M : H_n(q) → ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.JonesMarkovTrace","kind":"structure","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L75-L176","doc":"**Jones–Markov Trace** (Jones, 1987, Theorem 5.1 & Corollary 5.3).\n\nExternal proof axiom: for each Hecke algebra H_n(q) with q not a\nroot of unity, there exists a unique trace functional satisfying\nthe Markov property, which is non-degenerate on every irreducible\nsummand.\n\nWe encode this as a structure whose fields are the properties\nproved in Jones (1987). The proof is taken as axiomatic — the\n`sorry` marks where Jones's 54-page proof would go.\n\n**Three key properties:**\n1. **Existence & uniqueness**: a trace satisfying normalisation,\n   cyclicity, and the Markov property tr(x T_n) = z tr(x); the\n   negative stabilisation tr(x T_n⁻¹) = z₋ tr(x),\n   z₋ = z − (q − q⁻¹), is forced by the Hecke quadratic relation.\n2. **Non-degeneracy**: the trace is nonzero on every irreducible\n   H_n(q)-module S_λ.\n3. **Link invariance**: the trace value depends only on the isotopy\n   class of the braid closure, yielding the Jones polynomial. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:jones-markov-trace","label":"thm:jones-markov-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.T","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Generators T_1, ..., T_{n-1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.one","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Unit element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.mul","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.q_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.q_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L63-L63","doc":"q ≠ 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.q","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Deformation parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.carrier","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Carrier type of H_n(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.n","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Number of strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebraData","kind":"structure","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L50-L71","doc":"Minimal Hecke algebra data needed for the Markov trace axiom.\nThe full structure is in `knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean`; this\nextracts only what the Jones theorem requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L45-L46","doc":"The formal Laurent inverse `q⁻¹ = T^{-1}` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.q_param","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L42-L43","doc":"The canonical indeterminate `q = T^1` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.R_q","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/jones-markov-trace.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0}]}